---
description: Run bSmart /project through the shared adapter. /role is deprecated.
alwaysApply: true
---

When the user uses `/project`, run `python3 bSmart-System/integrations/bsmart_client_adapter.py` with that command and the user's arguments. The adapter remembers this client's project between commands. Do not set environment variables and do not write a shared selector file. If the output asks for a handoff, run the command again with the user's wrap-up after `handoff:`. Reply with stdout unchanged. Never confirm rename, retire, or delete yourself. If `python3` is missing or fails, use `python` (or `py -3` on Windows). `/role` only prints a deprecation notice; run it the same way and do not create a role.

If the session already contains a `bSmart — Startup` block, do not run `bStart.py` again. Otherwise run `python3 bSmart-System/bStart.py` once before the first reply and preserve its startup lines. If `python3` is missing or fails, use `python bSmart-System/bStart.py` (or `py -3 bSmart-System/bStart.py` on Windows). If the startup output contains a bSmart news block, relay that news briefly in the same first reply, once, and do not repeat it later.

When the first reply preserves the bStart startup block, wrap that visible block in a fenced code block: a line of three backticks, the lines unchanged, then a line of three backticks. Do not set a language tag. Cursor’s Markdown renderer collapses single newlines; the fence is what keeps each line. Include the Hi, greeting, bSmart — Startup, any bSmart news block, agent, project, workstream, active projects, each Use: command-help line, and the short git and update status lines. Stop before Context files:. Leave loaded context files out of the visible reply. Do not replace the block with a custom greeting or a reduced summary.
